# 📊 Dataset

The project currently uses an Indian food nutrition dataset.

Example:

```csv
food,category,serving,calories,protein,carbs,fat,fiber
Roti,Bread,1 piece,100,3,15,3,2
Rice,Grains,1 bowl,200,4,45,0.5,1
Dal,Pulses,1 bowl,180,10,25,5,7
Rajma,Pulses,1 bowl,220,12,35,4,9
Chole,Pulses,1 bowl,270,12,40,7,10
Paneer,Dairy,100 g,265,18,6,20,0
Curd,Dairy,100 g,60,3.5,4.7,3.3,0
Poha,Breakfast,1 bowl,250,5,40,8,3
Upma,Breakfast,1 bowl,220,6,35,7,3
Idli,Breakfast,2 pieces,140,4,28,1,2
Dosa,Breakfast,1 piece,170,4,30,4,2
Paratha,Bread,1 piece,220,5,30,9,4
Samosa,Snack,1 piece,150,3,15,8,2
Biryani,Main Course,1 bowl,350,15,45,12,3
```

The dataset can later be expanded with:

* Breakfast foods
* Lunch foods
* Dinner foods
* Snacks
* Fruits
* Vegetables
* Salads
* Raita
* High-protein foods
* Egg-based foods
* Non-vegetarian foods
* Regional Indian dishes

