# ⚙️ Installation

## 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/indian-diet-ai.git
```

Go into the project:

```bash
cd indian-diet-ai
```

---

## 2. Create virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

Activate it on Windows:

```powershell
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

---

## 3. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# 🔐 Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root:

```env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key

QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
QDRANT_API_KEY=

API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Never upload `.env` to GitHub.

---

# 🗄️ Qdrant Setup

The project uses Qdrant for vector storage.

After preparing the dataset, run the ingestion script:

```bash
python backend/rag/ingestion.py
```

This process:

```text
CSV
 ↓
Food Records
 ↓
Text Documents
 ↓
Embeddings
 ↓
Qdrant Collection
```

The collection used by the project is:

```text
indian_foods
```

---

# ▶️ Running the Backend

Activate the virtual environment:

```powershell
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

Start FastAPI:

```bash
uvicorn backend.main:app --reload
```

Backend:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Swagger documentation:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
```

---

# 🖥️ Running Streamlit

Open another terminal.

Activate the environment:

```powershell
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

Run:

```bash
streamlit run frontend/app.py
```

The Streamlit application will open in your browser.

---

# 🔌 API Endpoints

## Health Check

```http
GET /
```

Example response:

```json
{
  "message": "Indian Diet AI API is running",
  "status": "success"
}
```

---

## Health

```http
GET /health
```

Response:

```json
{
  "status": "healthy"
}
```

---

## Calorie Calculator

```http
POST /api/calorie/calculate
```

Request:

```json
{
  "age": 24,
  "gender": "female",
  "height_cm": 160,
  "weight_kg": 65,
  "activity_level": "moderately_active",
  "goal": "weight_loss"
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "bmr": 1344,
  "tdee": 2083.2,
  "bmi": 25.39,
  "daily_calorie_target": 1683.2,
  "goal": "weight_loss"
}
```

---

## Food Search

```http
GET /api/food/search?query=paneer
```

Example response:

```json
{
  "query": "paneer",
  "results": [
    {
      "food": "Paneer",
      "category": "Dairy",
      "serving": "100 g",
      "nutrition": "...",
      "score": 0.92
    }
  ]
}
```

---

## AI Chat

```http
POST /api/chat
```

Request:

```json
{
  "query": "How many calories are in paneer?"
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "query": "How many calories are in paneer?",
  "answer": "..."
}
```

